{"name":"Star of Life","hex":"#057bc1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Star of Life","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A blue six-pointed star, outlined with a white border and usually featuring the rod of Asclepius in the center, used as a symbol of emergency medical services in multiple countries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Star_of_Life"}],"entries":[{"title":"Star of Life","blocks":[{"text":"The Star of Life is a symbol used to identify emergency medical services. It features a blue six-pointed star, outlined by a white border. The middle contains a Rod of Asclepius – an ancient symbol of medicine. The Star of Life can be found on ambulances, medical personnel uniforms, and other objects associated with emergency medicine or first aid. Elevators marked with the symbol indicate the lift is large enough to hold a stretcher. Medical bracelets or tags sometimes use the symbol to indicate that the bearer has a medical condition that emergency services may need to know."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Star_of_life2.svg/330px-Star_of_life2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_of_Life"},{"title":"Star","blocks":[{"text":"A star is a luminous spheroid of plasma held together by self-gravity. The nearest star to Earth is the Sun. Many other stars are visible to the naked eye at night; their immense distances from Earth make them appear as fixed points of light. The most prominent stars have been categorised into constellations and asterisms, and many of the brightest stars have proper names. Astronomers have assembled star catalogues that identify the known stars and provide standardized stellar designations. The observable universe contains an estimated 1022 to 1024 stars. Only about 4,000 of these stars are visible to the naked eye—all within the Milky Way galaxy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star"},{"title":"Life","blocks":[{"text":"Life is the capacity in matter, formed of one or more units called cells, for processes such as cell signalling, homeostasis, metabolism, cell growth, adaptation, response to stimuli, and reproduction. All life eventually reaches a state of death. Many philosophical definitions of living systems have been proposed, such as self-organising systems. Defining life is further complicated by viruses, which replicate only in host cells, and the possibility of extraterrestrial life, which could be very different from life on Earth. Life exists all over the Earth in air, water, and soil, with many ecosystems forming the biosphere. Some of these are harsh environments occupied only by extremophiles. The life in a particular ecosystem is called its biota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg/330px-Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/A_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg/500px-A_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/A_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg/1280px-A_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/A_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg/500px-A_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An ambulance motorcycle from Israel's United Hatzalah, combining the Star of David with the Star of Life.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_United_Hatzalah_ambucycle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/NTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg/250px-NTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/NTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg/500px-NTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/NTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg/250px-NTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANTFD_Cifu_Branch_BBW-0191_right_side_at_Mackay_Memorial_Hospital_20200217.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/2019-04-28_16_05_16_An_ambulance_leaving_Fairfax_County_Fire_and_Rescue_Department_Station_Number_15_in_Chantilly%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/250px-2019-04-28_16_05_16_An_ambulance_leaving_Fairfax_County_Fire_and_Rescue_Department_Station_Number_15_in_Chantilly%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/2019-04-28_16_05_16_An_ambulance_leaving_Fairfax_County_Fire_and_Rescue_Department_Station_Number_15_in_Chantilly%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2019-04-28_16_05_16_An_ambulance_leaving_Fairfax_County_Fire_and_Rescue_Department_Station_Number_15_in_Chantilly%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam